  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2026-11-23T14:04:26.443Z",
  "deleteID": null,
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "The open beta now has thumbs-up / thumbs-down buttons on every world, for you to rate worlds as high and low quality.  What I don't understand is: what do these buttons *do*?   Are we:\n\n- contributing towards a global ranking of total upvotes/downvotes across all users?\n\n- contributing towards a \"people like you liked\" algorithm that will show us things based on the ratings of people who rated worlds similarly to us?\n\n- contributing towards whether or not a world gets out of Labs?\n\n- contributing towards whether a world gets flagged for review/deletion?\n\n- contributing towards feedback that the world creator can see?\n\n- just being pacified by a sense that we're \"doing something\" about unwanted content while not actually changing anything besides an icon on our own client?",
